Short : Battlehawks 1942 Enhanced 2.0b: HD-Installer with Enhanced framerate
Type  : game/patch
Author: Vesuri, after Galahad / Fairlight (v1.0)

 Battlehawks 1942 Enhanced 2.0b (09.11.2026)

 This install applies to "Battlehawks 1942" (c) 1989 Lucasfilm Games, PAL
 original release v1.0.

 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad version 20.0 to be in the path.
 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 0.9 MB OtherMem, and the
 A500 Kickstart 1.3 image as described below.
 For Enhanced framerate a 68020 or later is recommended.

 Features (2.0b, by Vesuri):
 ---------------------------
 - Enhanced framerate (CUSTOM2=1, set in the installed icon; CUSTOM2=0 or
   unset keeps the original timing). The game's time follows real time at
   any frame rate: flight, combat, timers and the replay run at the speed the
   A500 was tuned for, and faster Amigas get up to 50 frames per second
   (68030/50 and faster). The renderer's point transform, horizon fill and
   overlay are faster. The menus move their selection by mouse distance.
 - Fast memory and caches: the game's code and data run from fast memory.
   The game writes code; the caches are kept consistent with it on every CPU,
   so the installed icon no longer sets NOCACHE.
 - The blitter is waited for before the game draws over what it cleared (grey
   characters in the message bar on fast CPUs).
 - One slave replaces v1.0's two; the installer no longer asks which.
 - From v1.0: the manual check is removed, quit with F10.

 History:
 --------
 2.0b (09.11.2026) Vesuri: the above. Source: github.com/Vesuri/whdload.
 1.0  (12.05.2003) Galahad / Fairlight: the original install (below).

 Galahad's v1.0 ReadMe follows.

Short : HD-Installer for Battlehawks 1942 - (c) 1989 Lucasfilm Games
Type  : game/patch
Author: Galahad / Fairlight (gldflt@blueyonder.co.uk)

 
 This install applies to "Battlehawks 1942" © 1989 Lucasfilm Games
 Slave requires WHDLoad V15+.
 SLOW Game needs 0.5 MB Of Chipmem & 2.0MB of Fastmem (for preload option)
 FAST Game needs 0.5 MB of Chipmem & 2.5MB of Fastmem (for preload option)
 Kickstart 1.3

 SUPPORTED VERSIONS
 ------------------
 
 - PAL Original Release v1.0

 FEATURES
 --------

 - Full Loading from HD 
 - Lame-o-Protect removed (Document Check)
 - Installer and nice Icons by Frank!
 - Manual included
 - Quit Option (F10 key)
 
Thanks to Mad Matt for the images
 
 
 EXTRA NOTES
 -----------

There are two included slaves.  The SLOW slave is the default installed
slave, because I feel the game is too fast using the other slave, but I
have included it for you all just in case you wish to experiment.

Nothing tricky, just the usage of Fast ram makes it a hell of a lot 
quicker! 

The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts"
and must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from an
A500 with tools like "GrabKick" or similar which can be found on Aminet.
If the image is the wrong version or altered in any way, WHDLoad will
quit with an appropriate error message. 

Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive 
"util/boot/skick343.lha" on Aminet.

Kindest Regards, Galahad & Frank & Mad Matt

END.